    <bpmn:process id="W_W4360" name="W4360. Live-Goods Sustainability, Pollinator/Native &amp; ESG Reporting" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Sustainability cycle; ESG report; strategy
Frequency: Annual + ongoing program
Volume: Live-goods sustainability program
Owner: Sustainability (VS-25) / Garden Buyer / ESG
Participants: Sustainability (VS-25), Garden Buyer, ESG, Marketing (VS-14), Compliance (VS-22), Strategy (VS-33)
Source: workflow W4360 — Live-Goods Sustainability, Pollinator/Native &amp; ESG Reporting</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4360_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4360_Lane1" name="Sustainability">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4360_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4360_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4360_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4360_Lane2" name="Garden Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4360_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4360_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4360_Start4" name="Sustainability cycle; ESG report; strategy">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4360_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4360_Task5" name="Sustainability/Garden set the live-goods sustainability program —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Sustainability/Garden set the live-goods sustainability program — pollinator-friendly/native species promotion, neonicotinoid/bee-harm reduction, peat-reduction, responsible sourcing, and green-waste diversion (W4355)
Responsible (R): Sustainability / Garden Buyer
Accountable (A): Sustainability Lead / Head of Merch
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4360_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4360_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4360_Task6" name="Garden Buyer/Sourcing implement sustainable sourcing preferences…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Garden Buyer/Sourcing implement sustainable sourcing preferences (native/pollinator-friendly, certified sustainable growers, reduced-pesticide), and label/promote to customers
Responsible (R): Garden Buyer / Sourcing / Marketing
Accountable (A): Head of Merch / CMO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4360_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4360_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4360_Task7" name="Sustainability/ESG report the live-goods sustainability outcome…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Sustainability/ESG report the live-goods sustainability outcome (native/pollinator share, diversion, reduced-pesticide) into the ESG narrative (VS-25) and board assurance (VS-36/VS-21)
Responsible (R): Sustainability / ESG / Leadership
Accountable (A): Sustainability Lead
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4360_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4360_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4360_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4360_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4360_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-667 (ensure controlled execution — Live-Goods Shrink, Markdown, Compliance &amp; Analytics (PA-145.3).) | - CTL-667: sustainable sourcing preferences applied; bee-harm reduction; diversion reported (VS-25)
Owner: Sustainability (VS-25) / Garden Buyer / ESG</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
